WEBVTT

00:01:59.625 --> 00:02:02.976
Now, considering that we humans produce

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.393
300 million tons of new plastic each year,

00:02:07.417 --> 00:02:09.934
I'd say that our plastic numbers

00:02:09.958 --> 00:02:12.667
are looking pretty
comparable to bacteria's.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:16.309
So, after noticing this

00:02:16.333 --> 00:02:18.643
and after learning
about all of the creative ways

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:20.684
that bacteria find food,

00:02:20.708 --> 00:02:22.893
I started to think:

00:02:22.917 --> 00:02:25.809
could bacteria in
plastic-polluted environments

00:02:25.833 --> 00:02:29.250
have figured out
how to use plastic for food?